  "closed_findings": [
    {
      "id": "P5-record-R1-zero-delay-cancellation",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "closed_by_source_review",
      "original": "A zero-extra-delay recording replay could invoke consecutive synchronous native tools without a real asyncio scheduling point. Cancellation could remain unprocessed until all steps had posted input.",
      "resolution": "_run_batch now awaits asyncio.sleep(0) before every synchronous/async tool dispatch. CancelledError propagates and prevents later steps. The shared recording gate remains held across recording replay waits and releases in finally, preventing concurrent record_start or another recording replay.",
      "regression": "Pure zero-delay cancellation case schedules cancellation after the first synchronous tool and asserts exactly one dispatch. A separate replay-gate case checks start refusal and cancellation release."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5-record-R1-whole-record-preflight",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "closed_by_source_review",
      "original": "A non-paste text suffix containing a composed character longer than20 UTF-16 units could pass Python validation and fail after a valid prefix had posted native input. Python pointer bounds also admitted maximum edges excluded by CGRectContainsPoint.",
      "resolution": "Native RuyiAutomationValidateText validates all text scalar/budget and composed-character limits before direct input. record.target(actions) reuses this validation and ChordKeys for the entire read-only preflight before any replay input. Python pointer and drag-start validation uses half-open bounds. prepare_recording deep-copies the untrusted recording before validation and expansion.",
      "regression": "Pure cases exercise full-action native preflight and half-open coordinates. The real recording fixture includes invalid chord and Unicode suffix rejection before prefix input."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5-record-R1-missing-macro-input",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "closed_by_source_review",
      "original": "Making steps optional for recording mode allowed macro_run() without either input to silently report an empty successful replay.",
      "resolution": "The authored branch now returns invalid_args when steps is None. Explicit steps=[] retains the prior empty-macro behavior.",
      "regression": "Pure missing-both versus explicit-empty-steps case."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5-record-R1-save-fd-cleanup",
      "priority": "P3",
      "status": "closed_by_source_review",
      "original": "A failed temporary-file unlink during _save finally could raise before os.close(directory), leaking the anchored directory descriptor.",
      "resolution": "An outer finally closes the directory FD for every temporary-cleanup result.",
      "regression": "Pure cleanup-failure case makes unlink raise PermissionError and checks that close still runs."
    }
  ],
  "source_assessment": {
    "record_source": "The helper records only its own successful controlled_native_requests for keyboard.text/chord and mouse click/move/drag/scroll. It stores caller semantics after dispatch, excluding query calls and internal paste-generated keys. Version/target are removed and the native session removes its transport id before dispatch. The document keeps application identity and bounds instead of expired private refs/PIDs. Physical manual-input listening is a separate future scope.",
    "native_lifecycle_and_timer": "Recorder state is owned by the persistent native input worker. Protocol frames are serialized and the reader waits for completion before the next frame. The timer and request handlers run on the main loop. The timer may run while an input Wait services the run loop, but refresh only checks target/state and latches the first end reason. It does not collect/clear the action array or start a new recording. Collection occurs in the serialized record.stop frame. Before/after request refresh and the one-second timer enforce deadline/permission/secure/focus/identity/geometry checks. EOF and stop signals reuse existing input release, clipboard restoration and process exit cleanup.",
    "limits_and_partial": "Native capture bounds are1–300 seconds,100 actions and48000 action JSON bytes. A failed/partial native request, lock, permission loss, secure input, target/app change, timeout or capacity end produces complete=false with a reason and a retained collected prefix. Replay and persistence reject incomplete documents. A request may still have posted input before its failure, so incomplete means an interrupted recording rather than a complete account of business effects. The complete field now uses explicit @YES/@NO for real JSON booleans.",
    "whole_document_and_binding": "Python validates strict schema/platform/source/coordinate space, application fields, bounded actions/bytes, per-op field allowlists, finite monotone at/ended values, numeric limits and pointer half-open bounds before native preflight. Native read-only preflight reuses actual chord and full text validators. Then current native target, exact application executable/bundle and recorded size are required. Moved-window points are translated by origin delta, and each step retains the canonical registered tool/native focus/identity/geometry/hit guard.",
    "replay_semantics_and_registry": "Recording and authored steps are mutually exclusive. Missing input is refused. Replay maps to the existing live registry, checks every expanded canonical tool before dispatch, refuses hidden/missing tools, keeps explicit paste choice and text body, and expands recorded enters into guarded press_key calls. Idle gaps use next.at minus previous.ended, with gaps above0.3s capped at5s. Recording defaults to zero additional delay while authored steps retain120ms. Expanded replay is capped at200 steps. The recording gate blocks record_start throughout replay, and native recording_pending blocks replay of an active/uncollected recording.",
    "start_stop_and_readiness": "Start is a synchronous serialized native state request with a complete target and StrictFloat/StrictInt duration, preserving boolean rejection through FastMCP validation. record_start discovery follows actual recordReady, including input authorization and secure/unlocked state. stop remains callable to collect a recording after readiness is lost. Diagnostics reports controlled_native_requests and separate native installed/supported/ready status. Listing remains a local internal-file operation.",
    "save_and_listing": "save_as is validated before consuming native state. Save uses a nofollow directory FD, exclusive0600 temporary file, file flush/fsync, atomic relative replace and directory fsync. Cleanup now always closes the directory FD. The full collected recording remains in the response after errors, with saved=null rather than a false no-file claim after possible post-replace failure. Listing collects at most201 matching names, returns at most200 entries, opens nofollow/nonblocking files through the anchored directory, checks regular-file/size/read state, validates documents and marks invalid/symlink/FIFO/legacy incompatible files without replaying them.",
    "Windows_compatibility": "The Windows recording module is byte-identical to the baseline. batch_actions and wait ASTs are unchanged. _run_batch differs only by the intentional per-step cancellation checkpoint. Authored macro_run behavior preserves ordinary calls and default/explicit delay semantics while its added recording mode is Mac-only.",
    "fixture_and_documentation": "The dedicated native fixture adds only RUYI_RECORD_FIXTURE move/resize/secure commands. The recording E2E checks exact Chinese body+Enter, six native verbs, preserved clipboard formats, moved-window rebinding, invalid suffixes, failed dispatch, focus/deadline/secure/geometry/capacity and cleanup. App recording mode uses the normal LaunchServices App HTTP path and receiver readbacks. Shared tests now match the implemented record module/readiness instead of stale unsupported assertions. The record README separates controlled-call recording, partial results, later physical listening and original environment gates."
  },
  "compatibility_checks": {
    "windows_record_module_byte_identical": true,
    "batch_actions_public_AST_equal": true,
    "wait_AST_equal": true,
    "run_batch_AST_equal_after_removing_only_new_cancellation_checkpoint": true,
    "macro_run_source_assessment": "The public signature adds optional recording/target. Authored steps retain120ms when delay_ms is omitted and honor explicit delays. Explicit empty steps stay valid. Missing both inputs is an error. Windows rejects Mac recording-mode arguments before importing or dispatching native recording code."
  },
